# ==============================================================================
# ETAPA IV | Descriptiva de la cohorte y arbol de decision del patotipo sinovial
# Master's Thesis in Bioinformatics | Victor Daniel Velasco Perez
#
# Input   data/metadata_STRAP_local_xlx.txt      (SDRF de ArrayExpress)
#         resultados/etapa_3/datos/todos_resultados.rds
#         resultados/etapa_3/tablas/T_poblaciones_fiables.csv   (opcional)
# Output  resultados/etapa_4/{graficos, tablas, datos}
# Style   tidyverse style guide; seed 42
#
# The script reads the submission file directly and derives everything it needs,
# so it introduces no new data dependency.
#
# The acr20_response field of the submission reports five responders out of 208
# where the trial publishes 133. It is discarded here and no contrast is run
# against it, following the supervisor's instruction.
#
# WHAT THE PATHOTYPE IS. It is not a clinical variable and it is not a cluster.
# A pathologist stains four sequential sections of the biopsy for CD20 (B
# cells), CD3 (T cells), CD138 (plasma cells) and CD68 (sublining macrophages),
# grades each on a semiquantitative scale from 0 to 4, and applies a fixed rule:
#   lympho-myeloid  CD20 >= 2 and/or CD138 > 2
#   diffuse-myeloid CD68SL >= 2 with CD20 <= 1 and CD138 <= 2
#   pauci-immune    CD68SL < 2 and CD3, CD20, CD138 all < 1
# The grade is therefore a deterministic function of four cell abundances read
# under a microscope, which is exactly what deconvolution tries to estimate from
# expression. The trees below ask whether the computational estimate recovers
# that reading, and whether the clinical phenotype carries the same information.
#
# HONESTY OF THE ESTIMATE. A tree read on the observations that trained it
# reports memorisation. Every accuracy reported here comes from repeated
# stratified cross-validation with the complexity parameter tuned inside each
# training fold. The tree that is drawn is fitted on the full cohort for
# interpretation only, and its apparent accuracy is never reported as
# performance.
# ==============================================================================

